      "tests": [
        {
          "id": "mms_column_flux_bc_decay",
          "description": "Manufactured solution u(z,t) = z + exp(-alpha pi^2 t) cos(pi z), alpha = 0.01, on the quadratic-stretch column, prescribed K du/dz = alpha at both interfaces. The t=0 assertion pins the ic wiring; the t=0.1 assertion bounds the L2 error at the default NLEV = 64, which equals heat_1d_nonuniform_neumann's n=64 golden (5.40e-6) because the ramp is discretely exact and the constant coefficient reduces the operator to alpha times the plain nonuniform Laplacian. Per-resolution errors are pinned in tests/conformance/convergence/heat_column_varcoeff_flux_bc/golden/errors.json.",
